        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "704c05cb-317a-5075-8ffc-011904077f5b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Madman's Return, \"Rhythm Is a Dancer\", \"Colour of Love\", \"Good Fun\", \"The Music's Got Me\", \"Move to the Rhythm\", \"Rhythm Is A Dancer (2003)\"\n- People/Groups: Snap!, Bass Bumpers, CJ Stone, Bad Habit Boys\n- Topics: chart performance, releases, collaborations\n\nFacts:\n- In December 1991, \"Colour of Love\" was released as the first single from Snap!'s second studio album, The Madman's Return.\n- In 1992, Bass Bumpers' song \"The Music's Got Me\" reached number 36 on Billboard's Hot Dance Club Songs chart.\n- The Madman's Return is Snap!'s second studio album.\n- The Madman's Return contains Snap!'s international hit \"Rhythm Is a Dancer\".\n- \"Rhythm Is a Dancer\" is a song recorded by the German group Snap!.\n- \"Rhythm Is a Dancer\" reached number 1 in France, Ireland, Italy, the Netherlands, Germany, and the United Kingdom, and peaked at number 5 in the United States.\n- Bass Bumpers were also known as CJ Stone and Bad Habit Boys.\n- Bass Bumpers produced hits including \"Good Fun\", \"The Music's Got Me\", \"Move to the Rhythm\", and \"Rhythm Is A Dancer (2003)\" with Snap!.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "329af076-a1e5-5b55-bdee-51ad9f1aeeac",
        "text": "Page: The Madman's Return. Sentence: The Madman's Return is Snap!\nPage: The Madman's Return. Sentence: 's second studio album and contains the international massive hit \"Rhythm Is a Dancer\", which reached No. 1 in France, Ireland, Italy, the Netherlands, Germany and the United Kingdom and peaked at No. 5 in the US.\nPage: Rhythm Is a Dancer. Sentence: \"Rhythm Is a Dancer\" is a song recorded by German group Snap!\nPage: Colour of Love (Snap song). Sentence: It was released as the first single from their second studio album, \"The Madman's Return\" in December 1991.\nPage: Bass Bumpers. Sentence: Also known as Bass Bumpers, CJ Stone, and Bad Habit Boys, they produced their own hits such as \"Good Fun\", \"The Music's Got Me\" (a number 36 hit on \"Billboard's\" Hot Dance Club Songs chart in 1992), \"Move to the Rhythm\" and \"Rhythm Is A Dancer (2003)\" with Snap!\nPage: Bass Bumpers. Sentence: .",
